AN ORDINANCE OF TREUTLEN COUNTY, GEORGIA TO BE KNOWN AS THE “TREUTLEN COUNTY PEDDLER ORDINANC ”, ENACTED TO CREATE AND ESTABLISH RULES AND REGULATIONS FOR LICENSING DOOR TO DOOR PEDDLERS AND SOLICITORS WITHIN THE UNINCORPORATED AREA OF TREUTLEN COUNTY, GEORGIA.

WHEREAS, the Constitution of the State of Georgia, approved by the voters of the State in November 1982, and effective July 1, 1983, provides in Article IX, Section 11, Paragraph 1 thereof, that the governing authority of a County may adopt clearly reasonable ordinances, resolutions and regulations; and

WHEREAS, O.C.G.A. §48-13-9 provides that a local government may charge a regulatory fee for certain businesses, including peddlers; and

WHEREAS, the Board of Commissioners of Treutlen County, Georgia, has determined that there has been an increase in door-to-door solicitations in Treutlen County, Georgia and that such solicitation carries with it the growing threat of abusive techniques being used by such solicitors, canvassers and peddlers; and

WHEREAS, the Board of Commissioners of Treutlen County has determined that door-to-door solicitation and peddling and canvassing can be used as a pretext for inspecting a premises or the occupations thereof in anticipation of future criminal activity at the residence of the premises; and

WHEREAS, the Board of Commissioners of Treutlen County deems it necessary to protect the health, safety and welfare of the citizens of Treutlen County by regulating commercial door-to-door solicitation, peddling and canvassing;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED AND ORDAINED by the Board of Commissioners of Treutlen County, Georgia, and it is hereby resolved and ordained by the authority of same that the following ordinance, known as “Treutlen County Peddler Ordinance” is hereby enacted, with the following terms, limitations, and conditions:

SECTION ONE: Requirement of Permits for all Peddlers and Persons Soliciting

- (a) Any peddler desiring to sell any merchandise, article or other good or service or transact any other business within the unincorporated area of Treutlen County, Georgia, shall first register with the Treutlen County Sheriff, by completing a personal information questionnaire as set forth in Section Two of this ordinance and obtaining a personal identification card which shall serve as the permit to engage in the proscribed activities, and shall pay any necessary fees required by this ordinance. No form of solicitation, selling, or peddling may occur within the unincorporated area of Treutlen County, Georgia without prior registration, approval by the Treutlen County Sheriff, and the payment of those fees designated.

- (b) All peddlers must specify the location and duration of said activity, so as to determine that the preferred location is not in violation of any other applicable ordinance or deemed to be unsafe by the Treutlen County Sheriff.

- (c) No peddler shall attempt to sell any merchandise, article or other good or service or transact any other legal business on any street, sidewalk, park, parkway or any other public place unless the peddler’s license specifies that peddling in such public place is permitted.

SECTION TWO: Contents of Information Questionnaire

- (a) The Treutlen County Sheriff's Department shall prepare a questionnaire to be completed by each applicant for a fee of twenty-five ($25.00) dollars, payable to the Treutlen County Sheriff, seeking the issuance of a personal identification card and permit requiring pertinent information regarding the physical description, identity, and background of each application including, but not limited to, the following:

- (1) | Name and Social Security Number of individual applicant;

- (2) Date of Birth;

- (3) Driver’s License Number, if applicable;

- (4) Gender;

- (5) Residential address and primary telephone number;

- (6) Business address and telephone number;

- (7) Height and Weight;

- (8) Hair and eye color;

- (9) Name and address of organization represented and whether that organization is either: a. Commercial; or b. Non-commercial (including religious, charitable, and non-profit);

- (10) Name, address, and telephone number of the applicant’s immediate supervisor in the organization represented;

- (11) A list of any pleas of guilty, convictions, or sentences of probation entered against the application in regard to any offenses other than minor traffic violations;

- (b) The questionnaire form shall also bear the following statement:

“Georgia Law provides it is a felony to knowingly and willfully make a false, fictitious or fraudulent statement or representation in any matter within the jurisdiction of any department or agency of the government of any county of this state.”

- (c) The Treutlen County Sheriff shall review the questionnaire for the purpose of ascertaining whether the applicant has plead to, or been convicted of a felony, or a misdemeanor involving a violation of moral turpitude. After ascertaining that the questionnaire has been properly completed and that the applicant has not been disqualified by virtue of prior pleas or convictions of any felonies or misdemeanors involving violence or moral turpitude, the Treutlen County Sheriff, or his duly designated deputy, shall approve the application subject to the payment of any applicable license fee.

- (d) No individual shall be permitted to solicit sales, funds, contributions or donations within the unincorporated area of Treutlen County, Georgia, on behalf of any organization if the organization has had its questionnaire or permit revoked or denied under this article.

